{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'enterprises' %}{% set plan_short = 'Enterprises' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Priority 3' %}
{% set plan_title = 'Enterprises that return value to members' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Give every Nation-owned business a clear mandate, independent oversight and a quarterly account of capital, debt, jobs, contracts, repayments and returns.' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">The outcome</p><h2>Businesses are judged by results, not announcements.</h2><p class="plan-lede">Each company exists for a stated reason and reports against it. Commercial confidentiality protects real negotiating interests, not the basic account owed to the Nation as owner.</p></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>Purpose</h3><p>Every company has an owner-approved mandate and benefit target.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Separation</h3><p>Ownership, board oversight and daily management have distinct roles.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Return</h3><p>Capital is tracked to repayment, dividends, assets, jobs and training.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Year One commitments</p><h2>Build one enterprise governance system.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Complete company register</h3><p>Publish the legal entity, ownership, mandate, board, officers and relationship to the Nation.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Owner expectations</h3><p>Set annual targets for finance, member employment, procurement, training, safety and reporting.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Business-case gate</h3><p>Require options, valuation, financing, downside, conflicts, exit route and member benefit before new capital.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Board standard</h3><p>Use skills matrices, term limits, attendance records, evaluations and conflict procedures.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Quarterly company report</h3><p>Report revenue, operating result, cash, debt, Nation capital, repayments, jobs, contracts and major risks.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Correction and exit rules</h3><p>Set triggers for recovery plans, leadership change, restructuring, sale or closure.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Quarterly measures</p><h2>One comparable report for every company.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Finance</th><th>Member benefit</th><th>Governance</th><th>Risk</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Revenue, operating result, cash and debt</td><td>Member jobs, apprenticeships and procurement</td><td>Board attendance, vacancies and conflicts</td><td>Top risks and corrective action</td></tr><tr><td>Nation capital, repayments and dividends</td><td>Community service or strategic benefit</td><td>Targets met and missed</td><td>Guarantees, security and covenant status</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Decisions members make</h2><ul><li>What benefits count when a company does not pay a dividend?</li><li>How much Nation capital can one company receive without direct member approval?</li><li>How independent should boards be from elected leadership?</li><li>When does a weak result require correction, sale or closure?</li></ul></section>
<div class="plan-next"><a href="/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan/community-wealth">← Community wealth</a><a href="/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan/homes-infrastructure">Next: Homes and infrastructure →</a></div>
{% endblock %}
